From: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:30:19 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm/damon/core: cleanup damos->walk_completed in
 damos_walk_cancel()

DAMOS walk could be unexpectedly partially performed when there are
multiple schemes and the walk is requested after the previous walk is
canceled.

The expectation of DAMOS walk for a setup that having multiple schemes
is that it will walk for one snapshot for all schemes.  To know if the
walk for the one snapshot of a given scheme is done, each damos struct
has walk_completed field.  It is set when the walk for the given scheme
is completed.  The walk skips schemes having the field set.  It is reset
for all schemes when all the scheme got it set.

damos_walk_cancel() cancels all existing walks.  But it does not reset
the walk_completed field.  damos_walk_cancel() can be called at any
kdamond loop iteration.  For example, due to DAMON context pause or
DAMOS watermarks-caused deactivation.  It means that the function can
be called while only some of the schemes completed their walks.  And
users could request another walk after the canceled walk.  In the case,
because some of the schemes still have walk_completed set, the walk for
them is skipped.  As a result, DAMOS walk based user operations such as
update_schemes_tried_bytes kdamond command could show incomplete output.

Fix by unsetting the fields of all schemes in damos_walk_cancel().

The issue is found from Sashiko bug database.

Closes: https://sashiko.dev/#/bug/linux-228a4c52-0545-4c1f-90ce-41114d8272e9
Fixes: bf0eaba0ff9c ("mm/damon/core: implement damos_walk()")
Cc: <stable@vger.kernel.org> # 6.14.x
Signed-off-by: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
---
 mm/damon/core.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mm/damon/core.c b/mm/damon/core.c
index bb1739cb68cac..a4dcf273f5564 100644
--- a/mm/damon/core.c
+++ b/mm/damon/core.c
@@ -3033,6 +3033,7 @@ static void damos_walk_complete(struct damon_ctx *ctx, struct damos *s)
 static void damos_walk_cancel(struct damon_ctx *ctx)
 {
 	struct damos_walk_control *control;
+	struct damos *s;
 
 	mutex_lock(&ctx->walk_control_lock);
 	control = ctx->walk_control;
@@ -3040,6 +3041,9 @@ static void damos_walk_cancel(struct damon_ctx *ctx)
 
 	if (!control)
 		return;
+
+	damon_for_each_scheme(s, ctx)
+		s->walk_completed = false;
 	control->canceled = true;
 	complete(&control->completion);
 	mutex_lock(&ctx->walk_control_lock);
-- 
2.47.3

